        "kinetics:tbhp_wpo4",
        "experiment:tbhp_wpo4:2.2-1.5-70",
        "experiment:tbhp_wpo4:2.2-1.5-80"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "text": "At fixed instantaneous concentrations, heating from the lower to the higher temperature multiplies the main rate by 2.729 and the side rate by 2.705. These are rate multipliers, not final-yield multipliers.",
      "role": "explanation",
      "required": true,
      "evidence_ids": [
        "kinetics:tbhp_wpo4",
        "experiment:tbhp_wpo4:2.2-1.5-70",
        "experiment:tbhp_wpo4:2.2-1.5-80"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "text": "The concentration factor in the side/main rate ratio is catalyst^-0.765 × TBA^-0.260 × TBHP^0.953 × H2O2^-2.259. Competition changes as feedstocks are consumed and TBHP accumulates. The integrated side-reaction consumption of TBHP is 0.2427 and 0.4035 mol/L at the lower and higher temperatures, respectively.",
      "role": "explanation",
      "required": true,
      "evidence_ids": [
        "kinetics:tbhp_wpo4",
        "experiment:tbhp_wpo4:2.2-1.5-70",
        "experiment:tbhp_wpo4:2.2-1.5-80"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "text": "For this endpoint, 70 °C gives higher predicted selectivity. Temperature and residence time should be screened together. At the higher temperature, the predicted TBHP maximum is at approximately 1056.0 s on a 8.6-s grid; longer residence does not necessarily increase target yield.",
